# Frontend Stack & Conventions

## UI Components — shadcn/ui

- **Always use shadcn/ui** for UI components. Never hand-write buttons, inputs, cards, badges, etc.
- Components live in `apps/web/src/components/ui/` — these are shadcn-managed, do not edit directly
- To add new shadcn components: `npx shadcn@latest add <component>` (run from `apps/web/`)
- Already installed: `Button`, `Input`, `Card`, `Badge`, `Separator`, `Tooltip`, `Sheet`, `ScrollArea`, `Avatar`, `Skeleton`, `Sidebar`
- Custom/composed components go in `apps/web/src/components/` (not in `ui/`)
- Use the `cn()` utility from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — use shadcn/ui components
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';
import { Card, CardHeader, CardTitle, CardContent } from '@/components/ui/card';

// ❌ BAD — don't hand-write UI primitives
<button className="bg-blue-500 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded">Click</button>
```

## Icons — Lucide React

- **Always use `lucide-react`** for icons. No other icon library.
- Import individual icons, never the entire library.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
import { Search, Send, Database } from 'lucide-react';

// ❌ BAD
import * as Icons from 'lucide-react';
```

## Global State — Jotai

- **Use Jotai** for all global/shared state. No Redux, Zustand, or React Context for state.
- Atoms are defined in `apps/web/src/store/` — one file per domain (ask, sources, content, ui)
- Export atoms from `@/store` barrel file
- The `JotaiProvider` wraps the app in `apps/web/src/components/providers.tsx`

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — define atoms in store files
// src/store/ask.ts
import { atom } from 'jotai';
export const queryAtom = atom('');

// Use in components
import { useAtom } from 'jotai';
import { queryAtom } from '@/store';
const [query, setQuery] = useAtom(queryAtom);
```

## Styling — Tailwind CSS 4

- Use Tailwind utility classes for all styling. No CSS modules, styled-components, or inline styles.
- Theme colors are CSS variables defined in `globals.css` — use semantic names: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-card`, `border-border`, etc.
- Dark mode uses the `.dark` class strategy (not media query)
- The `cn()` helper merges Tailwind classes: `cn('base-class', conditional && 'active-class')`

## Routing — Next.js App Router

- Pages live in `apps/web/src/app/` using the App Router file convention
- Client components must have `'use client'` directive at the top
- API calls go through `apps/web/src/lib/api.ts` — never call fetch directly in components
